# Mesh Hop (P2b, the shell): Home is a list (Chats, Contacts, Settings, with a chevron and a short state each), the header has the
# Esc button, the caption line says the board and the notices; a page has the same header and its Esc goes back to Home, where it
# asks "Quit Mesh Hop?". The page bodies are still a 640 px column (the stage) centred under the shell. At the five sizes, no
# board (the app offline). Taps go by label (a first tap on a Home row selects it, the second opens it), a tap beside the stage does
# nothing, the keys come through the shared keyboard bridge. No shot or layout check here: the shared size rules (rows 7 mm,
# buttons 9 mm) fail on every control of the page bodies until the pages are converted; mesh-hop-script `check`
# (tests/flows/shell.script) holds the shell, which is outside the stage, to them.
title Mesh Hop: Home and the shell at five sizes
env MESHHOP_DATA /tmp/mesh-hop-scene-data
env MESHHOP_PORT /nonexistent/ttyMH
env MESHHOP_ONLINE 0
sizes 640x480 800x480 720x720 1024x600 1280x720

wait 900
expect text "Chats"
expect text "Contacts"
expect text "Settings"
expect text "Esc"
expect notext "Map"
expect notext "Terminal"
expect notext "Zero-hop"
expect noquit

# Contacts from Home: a first tap selects the row, the second opens it
tap "Contacts"
tap "Contacts"
wait 400
expect text "Zero-hop"

# beside the stage (the letterbox): nothing happens
@800x480 tapxy 0.03 0.5
@720x720 tapxy 0.5 0.95
@1024x600 tapxy 0.05 0.5
@1280x720 tapxy 0.05 0.5
expect text "Zero-hop"

# the Esc button of a page goes back to Home
tap "Esc"
wait 400
expect notext "Zero-hop"
expect text "Settings"

# Settings, a row of its list opens the packet log (a sub-page); the header Esc goes back to Settings, then Home
tap "Settings"
tap "Settings"
wait 400
expect text "Node name"
tap "Packet log"
wait 300
expect text "Clear"
tap "Esc"
wait 400
expect notext "Clear"
expect text "Node name"

# the keys through cp0_lvgl's queue and the app's key bridge: Tab goes to the next page (Settings -> Chats -> Contacts)
key tab
key tab
expect text "Zero-hop"
# Esc of the keyboard goes back to Home; a second short Esc at Home never quits: it says how to leave (in the caption line)
key esc
wait 300
expect notext "Zero-hop"
key esc
expect text "Hold Esc 3 s to exit"
expect noquit

# the header's Esc at Home asks first: Cancel stays, Quit leaves (a touch-only board has no other way out)
tap "Esc"
wait 600
expect text "Quit Mesh Hop?"
expect noquit
tap "Cancel"
wait 400
expect notext "Quit Mesh Hop?"
expect noquit
tap "Esc"
wait 600
expect text "Quit Mesh Hop?"
tap "Quit"
wait 400
expect quit
